<%- include('partials/head') %>

<section class="page-head">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>About Africa KNXION</h1>
    <p>Our vision for connecting the African community across the United States.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container container-narrow">
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>Our mission</h2>
      <p>Africa KNXION is a platform built to connect members of the African community across the <strong>United States</strong>. By registering with your <strong>name, contact details, profession</strong> and <strong>US state</strong>, you become part of a living network where people help each other directly — wherever they are.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <div class="feature-list">
        <div class="feature">
          <h3>1. Register your profile</h3>
          <p>Create a free account with your name, contact, profession and US state. Join the member directory.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <h3>2. Offer your services</h3>
          <p>Professionals publish the services they provide — plumbing, design, IT, fashion and more.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <h3>3. Request what you need</h3>
          <p>Ask for the services you need directly. Open requests are visible to the whole community.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature">
          <h3>4. Connect and review</h3>
          <p>Reach out directly, get the job done, and leave reviews so the community can trust one another.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>Why "KNXION"?</h2>
      <p>KNXION draws on the idea of <em>connection</em> — the links that bind a community together. It reflects the spirit of Ubuntu: <em>"I am because we are."</em></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
